  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": 1,
  "section_notes": "S2 removes any sales stop: a model above 5% only triggers notification and corrective action, which protects the Hearth 10 but gives purchasers full per-model failure rates. S5 makes recall discretionary with an open corrective-action alternative and no mandatory numeric recall, which favours Halcyon's Ember 8. S1 sets a 5-business-day reporting window for all incidents, which is weaker than the safe benchmark and benefits both companies given their unreported incidents."
